---
# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  DEFERRED — WP11 stage 5. Do not enable until stage 4 has been live and   ║
# ║  quiet for at least one week and every human account has enrolled.        ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
#
# Same two gates as stage 4: rename off `.DEFERRED`, and add
# `authentik-blueprint-mfa-required-all` to `blueprints.configMaps` in
# ../../values.yaml. Neither happens by accident.
#
# ── WHAT IT DOES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stage 4 left the flow with two validation stages: the enforcing one at order
# 25 gated on `platform-admins`, and the original inert `skip` stage at order
# 30 for everyone else. Stage 5 widens enforcement by removing the gates rather
# than by adding anything new — the stage that has already been proven in
# production for a week simply stops being group-scoped:
#
#   - delete the group policy binding on the order-25 binding  → it applies to
#     every user
#   - delete the negated group policy binding on order 30      → nothing left
#     to suppress
#   - delete the order-30 stage binding itself                 → otherwise
#     every user would be challenged twice, once per validation stage
#
# End state: one authenticator-validation stage, order 25, unconditional,
# `not_configured_action: configure` — a user with no device enrols inline and
# is then challenged. Nobody is refused, and nobody gets in on a password
# alone.
#
# Every entry uses `state: absent`, which authentik treats as idempotent: an
# absent entry whose object no longer exists is skipped, not an error. Running
# this twice is safe.
#
# ── ⚠ REQUIRED COMPANION EDIT — DO NOT SKIP ──────────────────────────────────
# `10-authentication-current-state.yaml` still declares the order-30 stage
# binding with `state: present`. If you enable this file without also removing
# the `binding-authentication-mfa-validation` entry from that file, the two
# blueprints will fight: one deletes the binding, the other recreates it, on
# every blueprint run, forever. Edit file 10 in the SAME commit that renames
# this one. File 10 is a snapshot of the authentication path; when you change
# the path, the snapshot has to move with it or git stops being the truth.
#
# ── OPTIONAL HARDENING, ONCE EVERYONE IS ENROLLED ────────────────────────────
# With every account holding a device, `not_configured_action` in
# 20-mfa-enrollment-optional.yaml can go from `configure` to `deny`. Only do
# this after `kubectl exec` confirms a device count equal to the count of
# active human users — the verification command is in README.md. `deny` with a
# gap between those two numbers is a lockout with extra steps.
#
# Consider renaming the stage from `platform-admin-mfa-validation` to something
# accurate once it applies to everyone. Renaming is a rename of the `name`
# identifier and will create a NEW stage rather than rename the existing one,
# so it is a stage-4-shaped change of its own. Leaving the name alone is the
# boring, correct choice.
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: authentik-blueprint-mfa-required-all
  namespace: authentik
  annotations:
    argocd.argoproj.io/sync-options: ServerSideApply=true
data:
  mfa-required-all.yaml: |
    version: 1
    metadata:
      name: InfraWeaver MFA Required — all users
      labels:
        blueprints.goauthentik.io/description: >-
          Removes the platform-admins scoping from the MFA validation stage
          and retires the original skip stage, so every user is challenged.
    entries:
      # ── 1. Un-scope the enforcing stage ───────────────────────────────────
      - model: authentik_policies.policybinding
        state: absent
        identifiers:
          target: !Find [authentik_policies.policybindingmodel, [flowstagebinding__stage__name, platform-admin-mfa-validation]]
          order: 0

      # ── 2. Drop the negated suppression on the legacy stage ───────────────
      - model: authentik_policies.policybinding
        state: absent
        identifiers:
          target: !Find [authentik_policies.policybindingmodel, [flowstagebinding__stage__name, default-authentication-mfa-validation]]
          order: 0

      # ── 3. Retire the legacy inert stage from the flow ────────────────────
      # The stage object itself is left in place, unbound — deleting it would
      # also delete any historical references and buys nothing.
      - model: authentik_flows.flowstagebinding
        state: absent
        identifiers:
          target: !Find [authentik_flows.flow, [slug, default-authentication-flow]]
          order: 30
